DESCRIPTION:The Interdisciplinary Rehabilitation Research Seminar Series i
 nvites faculty\, trainees\, students\, and staff across the School of Med
 icine to hear from experts advancing the science and practice of rehabili
 tation. This session will feature Raheleh Ghasseminia\, PhD\, MS\, OTR/L\
 , assistant professor in the Occupational Therapy Doctorate (OTD) Divisio
 n\, who will share insights from her research about "An Institutional Eth
 nography of Interdisciplinary Sexual Health Practice in SCI Rehabilitatio
 n." The series promotes interdisciplinary dialogue and collaboration to t
 ranslate innovative rehabilitation research into improved patient care.
